WEBVTT

00:07.530 --> 00:12.510
Hey, Kiriyama, doesn't it seem like 
Nagumo's been struggling lately?

00:12.510 --> 00:17.830
I'd have thought he'd be running away 
with it by the time the late game started.

00:17.830 --> 00:23.460
Top Group List
 Rank  Year  Group Name          Points
1         3rd    Nagumo Group      236 
2         2nd   Koenji Group         230
3         3rd    Kiriyama Group    188
4         3rd    Ochiai Group         167
5         3rd    Mizoe Group          166
6         2nd   Sakayanagi Group  161

00:18.160 --> 00:23.460
But he keeps putting off dealing with 
Koenji, and now they're neck-and-neck.

00:24.020 --> 00:27.580
No one expected Koenji to 
take this test seriously.

00:27.580 --> 00:32.970
He went from completely off our 
radar to the biggest threat we face.

00:33.350 --> 00:35.600
So, what do we do about it?

00:35.600 --> 00:39.050
I'll activate all the groups 
Nagumo left me in charge of.

00:39.050 --> 00:41.960
Are you serious? It's just one guy!

00:41.960 --> 00:44.230
Koenji's our only real threat.

00:44.540 --> 00:47.820
I'll take point on directing his takedown.

00:47.820 --> 00:49.220
You?

00:49.220 --> 00:50.570
Let me do it!

00:50.570 --> 00:53.700
I've gotta get in Nagumo's 
good graces, too!

00:53.700 --> 00:54.690
No.

00:55.770 --> 00:59.580
Nagumo and I are the only ones 
capable of stopping Koenji.

00:59.930 --> 01:02.440
Recognize that we're dealing 
with our ultimate enemy.

01:13.510 --> 01:19.310
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

02:23.390 --> 02:29.940
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

02:36.500 --> 02:37.520
What's the situation?

02:38.250 --> 02:40.590
He's fast asleep.

02:39.600 --> 02:42.010
<b>#14 The Extraordinary Prodigy</b>

02:40.590 --> 02:44.530
How about we surround him 
while he's still in his tent?

02:44.530 --> 02:47.650
And if someone were to see us, 
how would we explain ourselves?

02:47.650 --> 02:50.650
Don't forget, GPS searches 
aren't perfect, either.

02:52.650 --> 02:58.030
As initially discussed, we'll make 
our move as Koenji starts his travel.

02:58.310 --> 02:59.160
Let's go.

03:06.520 --> 03:09.550
Is there some way I can help you?

03:09.550 --> 03:13.670
We'd like you to remain 
in this spot for the day.

03:13.940 --> 03:19.300
I have no idea who you are, but you 
must realize I won't agree to that.

03:20.010 --> 03:22.910
I promise to make it worth your while.

03:23.290 --> 03:26.300
You'll have a far easier 
time at school with

03:26.300 --> 03:29.310
Student Council President 
Nagumo on your side.

03:30.680 --> 03:34.050
I'm in quite a hurry, 
so I'll just be going now!

03:34.950 --> 03:36.630
A-Are you kidding me?!

03:36.630 --> 03:38.350
Stay calm, Mikitani.

03:38.350 --> 03:41.240
How the hell can I be calm?! 
He just got away!

03:41.480 --> 03:47.870
He'll have trouble participating in 
challenges if he's focused on evading us.

03:47.870 --> 03:52.400
And if he does decide to try one, 
we can catch up to him there.

04:01.220 --> 04:03.650
You're taking a nap right 
after you shake us off?

04:03.650 --> 04:05.980
I guess you must be pretty exhausted.

04:05.980 --> 04:07.770
But of course.

04:07.770 --> 04:10.610
I'm just as human as you are.

04:11.220 --> 04:14.010
Why not take the whole day off, then?

04:14.010 --> 04:16.900
It's good advice from your senpai.

04:17.540 --> 04:21.370
Take the day off? 
What a funny thing to say.

04:24.490 --> 04:27.700
Do not think of me as an ordinary man.

04:27.700 --> 04:32.880
My stamina is already perfectly recovered!

04:33.260 --> 04:37.320
You've been running on all 
cylinders these last ten days.

04:37.320 --> 04:41.420
Even with superhuman stamina like yours, 
you should be reaching your limit.

04:41.420 --> 04:46.170
Sorry to disappoint, but I'm 
what's known as a short sleeper.

04:47.270 --> 04:48.940
A short sleeper...

04:49.280 --> 04:51.800
That's a serious problem if true.

04:52.300 --> 04:54.150
What's it mean, Kiriyama?

04:54.370 --> 04:55.790
A short sleeper is someone

04:55.790 --> 04:59.860
who can maintain perfect health with 
fewer hours of sleep than most people.

05:00.220 --> 05:06.160
In other words, he can fully recharge 
with only short breaks throughout the day.

05:06.480 --> 05:10.520
If you don't mind, I'm on my way 
to the next designated area.

05:11.340 --> 05:12.670
Hey, wait!

05:13.860 --> 05:16.040
Enough. We'll change tactics.

05:16.430 --> 05:19.670
We'll follow him and keep 
him out of challenges.

05:20.150 --> 05:23.550
I'm the leader here. 
Respect the chain of command.

05:37.990 --> 05:40.690
Koenji! Quit playing tough!

05:40.930 --> 05:43.330
Goodness, it's noisy here.

05:43.870 --> 05:47.660
Perhaps I'll have to up my pace!

05:48.490 --> 05:49.700
You're kidding me!

05:49.700 --> 05:51.380
Damn it. Go after him!

05:51.380 --> 05:53.340
Wait. That's not up to you.

05:53.340 --> 05:56.340
Shut up! I won't let him get away again!

05:57.710 --> 05:58.650
Honestly...

06:02.030 --> 06:04.610
The effort you're putting in is palpable.

06:04.960 --> 06:08.100
Like we give a damn about 
appearances right now!

06:08.380 --> 06:10.390
This is your last warning.

06:10.390 --> 06:12.080
Save it for tomorrow if you prefer.

06:12.080 --> 06:13.850
Just stay in place and don't do anything.

06:13.850 --> 06:17.310
H-Hey, Nagumo said to 
hold him down for two days!

06:17.310 --> 06:20.520
It's not wise to spend so long on Koenji.

06:20.520 --> 06:23.000
The eve of the last day 
is two days from now.

06:23.000 --> 06:26.370
We should focus on getting 
points of our own.

06:26.370 --> 06:30.340
Then we'll set small teams to watch 
and harry him for those two days!

06:30.340 --> 06:32.140
You think Koenji will let that happen?

06:32.140 --> 06:34.370
You just have to do it right!

06:34.600 --> 06:36.380
You think you can "do it right"?

06:38.040 --> 06:39.290
Hell yeah, I can!

06:39.290 --> 06:43.650
And I'm gonna want a ticket 
to Class A when I do!

06:45.050 --> 06:47.090
You heard all that, right?

06:47.090 --> 06:50.930
I want you to stay right here 
until the day after tomorrow.

06:51.460 --> 06:55.190
I fear I can't agree to that, 
but what happens when I refuse?

06:55.190 --> 06:58.690
We could have you expelled, for one.

06:59.180 --> 07:01.690
I don't take orders from anyone.

07:01.690 --> 07:05.320
I'll make sure you don't have a choice.

07:05.670 --> 07:10.110
Goodness me. 
This is hardly a beautiful situation.

07:10.110 --> 07:11.920
What'll you do, then?

07:11.920 --> 07:16.460
The minute you try to push us 
out of the way, it's game on.

07:17.550 --> 07:18.710
Is it really?

07:25.700 --> 07:28.140
I'll be going now.

07:33.980 --> 07:37.140
Ow! My arm! He broke my arm!

07:37.140 --> 07:40.060
What disgusting behavior, Koenji.

07:40.060 --> 07:42.440
You just crippled Moroka.

07:42.720 --> 07:44.880
Looks like he took a flop to me.

07:44.880 --> 07:49.820
Say what you want. 
You still pushed him!

07:49.820 --> 07:55.330
I show no mercy to those who 
attempt to halt my advance.

07:55.330 --> 07:59.330
And if we report this to the school?

07:59.330 --> 08:03.220
Admitting to ganging up 
on a younger student...

08:03.220 --> 08:05.960
Wouldn't that merely cement your disgrace?

08:09.470 --> 08:11.870
Would you kindly allow me to leave now?

08:11.870 --> 08:17.480
Entertaining your nonsense has put 
my arrival order reward at risk.

08:17.480 --> 08:20.600
Sorry, but you're not going anywhere.

08:20.830 --> 08:23.690
Ready to bare your fangs at me, then?

08:25.240 --> 08:27.090
Time is money!

08:27.400 --> 08:29.360
Just do it quickly.

08:29.610 --> 08:31.510
You sure about this, Mikitani?

08:31.510 --> 08:33.370
You're really gonna mess him up?

08:33.370 --> 08:38.640
Yeah. If it comes to it, 
I'll take him down with me.

08:38.640 --> 08:39.370
Let's go!

08:48.600 --> 08:49.630
Damn it!

09:02.500 --> 09:03.900
Damn it...

09:08.010 --> 09:11.360
Damn it... Who the hell are you?

09:11.710 --> 09:17.100
Wouldn't it have been easier 
to just shake us off?!

09:17.100 --> 09:20.870
Your constant company has 
been a thorn in my side.

09:20.870 --> 09:22.270
I see.

09:22.270 --> 09:26.880
Break their spirits by demonstrating 
your overwhelming superiority.

09:26.880 --> 09:29.280
I must be going now.

09:29.600 --> 09:32.200
Damn it. Who the hell is that guy?

09:32.200 --> 09:33.850
Is he even a high schooler?

09:34.650 --> 09:36.980
There are times in life when 
you'll have to deal with

09:36.980 --> 09:39.000
someone you didn't account for.

09:39.390 --> 09:40.880
Just like Nagumo.

09:41.450 --> 09:45.230
Hey... Are you gonna tell 
Nagumo that I failed?

09:45.600 --> 09:46.980
Don't worry.

09:46.980 --> 09:50.480
We knew from the start that 
Koenji was a rogue element.

09:50.480 --> 09:53.990
But everyone has a weak point.

09:54.600 --> 10:00.440
<i>Koenji will be convinced that the 
third-years are no threat to him.</i>

10:00.440 --> 10:02.190
<i>We'll use that against him.</i>

10:07.910 --> 10:08.880
Oh?

10:09.100 --> 10:11.380
If it isn't Ayanokoji-kun!

10:11.690 --> 10:14.030
You're looking better than I expected.

10:14.030 --> 10:16.760
Everyone's been working really hard.

10:17.100 --> 10:20.750
What about you? Are you 
taking care of yourself?

10:20.750 --> 10:23.630
Yeah, I'm feeling fine for now.

10:23.630 --> 10:25.630
I hope you'll be careful, though.

10:25.630 --> 10:29.270
You could always get hurt 
and have to drop out.

10:30.670 --> 10:32.460
Three days left, right?

10:32.460 --> 10:34.000
It appears so.

10:34.000 --> 10:34.780
Hey!

10:35.780 --> 10:37.530
It's you, Ayanokoji!

10:37.860 --> 10:40.490
Sorry to intrude on your class.

10:40.490 --> 10:42.350
Nah, it's great to have you!

10:42.350 --> 10:45.040
It's hard being the only guy around.

10:45.040 --> 10:47.770
Test's over for the day.

10:47.770 --> 10:49.920
Come camp out with us!

10:49.920 --> 10:51.920
What a lovely idea!

10:51.920 --> 10:53.440
Sounds fine to me.

10:53.440 --> 10:55.980
Ayanokoji-kun's got that harmless vibe.

10:55.980 --> 10:57.370
He really does!

11:07.790 --> 11:08.980
Senpai.

11:08.980 --> 11:10.520
Ayanokoji-senpai.

11:11.840 --> 11:14.320
It's me, Nanase.

11:15.510 --> 11:17.300
What brings you here at this hour?

11:17.670 --> 11:20.950
I have something urgent to tell you.

11:21.200 --> 11:26.330
It's about a major plan to force 
you to drop out of the test.

11:28.000 --> 11:32.490
Seems like you were having a 
grand ol' time with Ayanokoji.

11:32.490 --> 11:33.670
Anything to show for it?

11:33.670 --> 11:34.800
No.

11:35.190 --> 11:37.720
He proved to be beyond my ability.

11:38.650 --> 11:42.970
So you skipped the feminine wiles 
and took him on face-to-face, huh?

11:42.970 --> 11:45.730
"Feminine wiles"?

11:46.160 --> 11:47.980
Forget it.

11:47.980 --> 11:50.370
H-Hosen-kun...

11:51.650 --> 11:55.190
I'm K-Katagiri of Class C.

11:55.190 --> 11:56.900
Don't give a damn.

11:56.900 --> 11:58.480
What's the matter?

11:58.480 --> 12:02.780
I, um... brought something for Hosen-kun.

12:02.780 --> 12:05.790
This better be good, 
or I'll knock your teeth out.

12:05.790 --> 12:07.370
H-Here!

12:07.370 --> 12:10.130
It will let you talk to Utomiya-kun!

12:11.350 --> 12:12.880
What's up, man?

12:12.880 --> 12:14.380
You wanna play?

12:15.050 --> 12:17.650
I didn't want to contact you.

12:17.650 --> 12:20.890
But it's the only way 
to see my plan through.

12:20.890 --> 12:24.470
Plan, huh? What plan is this?

12:24.470 --> 12:29.290
<i>We're about to execute a plan 
that will save the first-years.</i>

12:29.290 --> 12:30.900
Who needs saving?

12:30.900 --> 12:36.400
Four first-year groups are 
currently in the bottom ten.

12:36.400 --> 12:39.780
Two of them are from our Class D.

12:40.560 --> 12:44.310
What's the big deal? 
Less garbage to deal with.

12:44.310 --> 12:46.880
You're not gonna ask me for help, are ya?

12:46.880 --> 12:48.900
<i>You're free to refuse.</i>

12:48.900 --> 12:51.760
<i>I just wanted to make sure you knew.</i>

12:51.760 --> 12:54.420
<i>I'll carry it out with or without you.</i>

12:54.420 --> 12:56.760
Sounds like we're done, then. Bye.

12:58.030 --> 13:01.410
You're saying you won't help, then?

13:01.410 --> 13:05.300
<i>Hold on. I never said I wouldn't help.</i>

13:05.300 --> 13:06.520
What?

13:06.800 --> 13:12.270
If you get on your knees and beg, 
I might be willing to lend a hand.

13:12.750 --> 13:15.600
Shut up. I would never beg you!

13:15.600 --> 13:18.110
<i>Conversation's over, then.</i>

13:18.110 --> 13:20.610
<i>You okay with that, Tsubaki?</i>

13:23.680 --> 13:27.620
Figures I couldn't leave 
this to Utomiya-kun.

13:27.620 --> 13:31.630
So? What's all this about 
saving first-years?

13:31.630 --> 13:36.020
You really wanna save 
everyone at the bottom?

13:36.460 --> 13:38.560
<i>First, let me ask you one thing.</i>

13:38.560 --> 13:41.630
<i>Can I assume Nanase-san's on our side?</i>

13:41.850 --> 13:43.130
For now, yeah.

13:43.130 --> 13:47.250
All right. Then I'll continue.

13:47.250 --> 13:50.390
You're right. I intend to save them all.

13:50.780 --> 13:54.800
<i>All grade years will work together, 
like the upperclassmen are doing.</i>

13:54.800 --> 13:59.650
<i>Groups at the bottom will be absorbed 
by groups with points to spare.</i>

13:59.650 --> 14:04.410
Not a bad offer. 
But that doesn't guarantee a win.

14:04.410 --> 14:05.580
<i>That's true.</i>

14:05.580 --> 14:11.350
<i>So we need to force upperclassmen groups 
to drop out before the final day ends.</i>

14:11.350 --> 14:12.210
What's that?

14:12.420 --> 14:16.290
There are still a number 
of single-person groups.

14:16.730 --> 14:18.960
We just have to take them down.

14:18.960 --> 14:21.000
Oh, I getcha.

14:21.000 --> 14:25.340
Forcing five groups out would 
save everyone for sure.

14:25.340 --> 14:29.750
<i>So, what was it you wanted me to do?</i>

14:29.750 --> 14:34.220
You were planning on taking 
Ayanokoji-senpai down, weren't you?

14:34.220 --> 14:38.630
But he's always on the move, so you 
haven't been able to catch him.

14:38.630 --> 14:41.610
But with a larger net, 
you might stand a better chance.

14:41.860 --> 14:47.820
So you'll surround Ayanokoji and hold 
him down in exchange for my help?

14:47.820 --> 14:48.630
<i>Yes.</i>

14:48.630 --> 14:50.740
I like how you think.

14:50.740 --> 14:52.910
<i>But the school staff ain't stupid.</i>

14:52.910 --> 14:55.530
If we're caught, both sides 
will be expelled for fighting.

14:55.530 --> 14:59.880
Then I'll take the bullet as 
ringleader of the whole affair.

15:01.430 --> 15:05.380
I don't have any reason 
to stay at this school.

15:05.380 --> 15:08.260
I'm pretty fine with quitting early.

15:11.990 --> 15:15.500
Suicide bombers are scary as hell.

15:15.500 --> 15:17.230
I'm impressed.

15:17.230 --> 15:19.120
Lemme check one more time.

15:19.120 --> 15:22.940
The plan to fight Ayanokoji 
to get him to drop out—

15:22.940 --> 15:26.610
you're saying you came up with 
it all by yourself, Tsubaki?

15:26.610 --> 15:28.610
<i>That's right.</i>

15:28.610 --> 15:32.120
<i>And if we're caught, 
I'll take responsibility.</i>

15:32.120 --> 15:34.620
So, when does this thing kick off?

15:34.620 --> 15:36.880
I can't tell you that yet.

15:36.880 --> 15:40.130
I don't want that information getting out.

15:40.130 --> 15:44.880
<i>It's fine if you wanna keep it secret, 
but I can't help you until I know.</i>

15:44.880 --> 15:48.390
<i>That's what the transceiver is for.</i>

15:48.640 --> 15:50.860
<i>I'll call again later. See ya.</i>

15:51.580 --> 15:54.070
Man, she's sharp.

15:54.070 --> 15:55.720
What will you do?

15:55.720 --> 15:59.650
Figure I'll play along for now.

15:59.650 --> 16:05.050
I get to have my fun, 
and Tsubaki takes the fall.

16:05.050 --> 16:07.280
Can't get much better than that.

16:08.480 --> 16:10.410
Thank you for telling me.

16:10.740 --> 16:13.140
You probably shouldn't stay here long.

16:13.140 --> 16:17.040
Right. If anything else happens, 
I'll let you know.

16:17.290 --> 16:19.840
No, you've done enough.

16:19.840 --> 16:23.110
You should devote the rest of your time

16:23.110 --> 16:25.550
to supporting the Hosen-Amasawa group.

16:26.080 --> 16:30.480
<i>If they lose trust in Nanase, 
she'll lose her usefulness to me.</i>

16:30.950 --> 16:33.550
If you insist, Ayanokoji-senpai.

16:34.090 --> 16:35.430
Very well.

16:36.180 --> 16:39.300
<i>I'm not surprised the 
first-years want to ambush me.</i>

16:39.870 --> 16:43.940
<i>It doesn't change my plan at all.</i>

16:44.810 --> 16:49.450
Can't believe we're climbing a 
mountain first thing in the morning!

16:46.190 --> 16:50.640
You said you were fine, 
but you're clearly out of breath!

16:49.450 --> 16:51.450
What do you expect?

16:51.450 --> 16:57.990
Ayanokoji-kun, have you felt lonely 
doing this test all by yourself?

16:57.990 --> 17:01.830
No, the freedom and 
flexibility override it.

17:01.830 --> 17:07.590
I think I would have 
felt lonely and scared.

17:07.830 --> 17:11.590
I can't picture you being 
afraid of anything.

17:11.860 --> 17:15.840
I'm really quite a fraidy-cat.

17:16.510 --> 17:21.860
I could never live on an island 
like Horikita-san or Ibuki-san,

17:21.860 --> 17:23.730
all by myself as a girl.

17:24.030 --> 17:27.440
Man, you two are thick as thieves!

17:27.440 --> 17:29.450
Just date already!

17:29.450 --> 17:32.550
Then you can come join our class! 'Kay?

17:32.550 --> 17:34.790
Just chill out already!

17:37.020 --> 17:39.960
Ishizaki-kun is funny, isn't he?

17:43.740 --> 17:45.660
We're this way.

17:45.660 --> 17:47.090
Guess that's it for our collab.

17:47.090 --> 17:50.300
Yes, there's not much test left.

17:50.300 --> 17:52.340
Keep your spirits up to the end.

17:52.340 --> 17:55.400
You, too, Ayanokoji-kun. Take care.

18:01.550 --> 18:04.060
What are you thinking, Tsubaki?

18:04.060 --> 18:07.800
Just doing a dry run in my head.

18:08.200 --> 18:09.190
Need something?

18:09.990 --> 18:14.070
Why are our conversations the only 
ones you don't use transceivers for?

18:14.940 --> 18:18.940
You're the only one I can trust.

18:18.940 --> 18:23.960
I wanted to talk to you directly 
and get your unfiltered opinion.

18:25.960 --> 18:30.210
Tsubaki-san, there's something 
I need to talk to you about.

18:30.210 --> 18:32.720
First, Yagami.

18:32.970 --> 18:36.520
Where did you go when you 
disappeared yesterday?

18:36.520 --> 18:42.230
Oh, sorry. My watch broke down, 
and I went back to the starting point.

18:42.230 --> 18:44.770
That's the second time you've 
had a watch breakdown.

18:44.770 --> 18:46.600
What are you planning?

18:46.820 --> 18:48.630
That's not nice.

18:48.630 --> 18:52.570
You had a breakdown of your 
own a few days ago, remember?

18:52.570 --> 18:54.740
Mine was just malfunctioning.

18:54.740 --> 18:57.120
So was mine!

18:57.120 --> 19:01.080
Could you guys argue some other time?

19:01.080 --> 19:03.250
Anyway, what did you want to talk about?

19:03.250 --> 19:07.460
I brought a present for you.

19:07.460 --> 19:08.710
What is it?

19:08.710 --> 19:12.010
I borrowed it from a group in my Class B.

19:12.010 --> 19:16.470
The person using this tablet is on 
the same table as Ayanokoji-senpai.

19:16.740 --> 19:23.350
So I can use that to know exactly 
where he is in real time?

19:23.620 --> 19:26.400
How do you know they're on the same table?

19:26.400 --> 19:31.890
You used repeated GPS searches 
to narrow it down, right?

19:31.890 --> 19:33.610
Exactly!

19:33.610 --> 19:35.630
Is this not appreciated, though?

19:35.630 --> 19:38.000
Nah, very much appreciated.

19:38.360 --> 19:39.620
But are you sure about this?

19:39.900 --> 19:42.360
We're all in this together.

19:42.360 --> 19:48.560
And you'll need this plan 
for insurance, right?

19:48.560 --> 19:49.880
Insurance?

19:49.880 --> 19:55.080
Plan A is attacking Ayanokoji-senpai 
and making him drop out.

19:55.080 --> 19:58.470
But on the off-chance that we fail,

19:58.470 --> 20:03.770
Plan B can be making him miss all his 
designated areas so he loses points.

20:04.080 --> 20:09.210
Hinder his movements so he's penalized 
for repeated missing of designated areas?

20:09.210 --> 20:13.150
And if my insurance strategy successfully 
takes him out of the game,

20:13.150 --> 20:19.070
how about I get five million of 
the 20-million-point reward?

20:19.980 --> 20:21.740
It's not a bad idea.

20:21.740 --> 20:23.840
What do you think, Tsubaki?

20:23.840 --> 20:26.290
I suppose it's worth pursuing.

20:26.650 --> 20:27.790
However...

20:28.190 --> 20:29.140
What's that?

20:29.140 --> 20:32.920
A tablet on the same table 
as Ayanokoji-senpai.

20:32.920 --> 20:35.420
What? When did you...

20:35.420 --> 20:38.570
You're even better than 
I thought, Tsubaki-san.

20:38.980 --> 20:42.600
You'd already thought up 
my insurance plan, then?

20:42.600 --> 20:45.810
Even so, why didn't you bring it up?

20:46.020 --> 20:52.310
I didn't like the fact that Yagami-kun 
thought up the same plan I did.

20:52.310 --> 20:57.820
I guess, under the circumstances, 
I can't accept any reward.

20:58.680 --> 20:59.950
Thank you.

21:02.570 --> 21:06.710
Tsubaki, do you really mean to 
take all the blame on yourself?

21:06.710 --> 21:12.210
I'm the one who initially wanted 
to get Ayanokoji-senpai expelled.

21:12.650 --> 21:15.780
You just went along with me, right?

21:16.200 --> 21:17.960
Well, yes.

21:18.590 --> 21:20.610
But are you sure I shouldn't 
be the one to go?

21:20.950 --> 21:24.850
I think I can beat Ayanokoji one-on-one.

21:24.850 --> 21:26.470
I can't allow that.

21:26.470 --> 21:30.230
Class C needs you, Utomiya-kun.

21:31.440 --> 21:32.450
Very well.

21:32.810 --> 21:36.200
I'll remain nearby and watch you fight.

21:38.680 --> 21:40.660
Attention, all groups.

21:41.020 --> 21:43.770
The enemy is moving to designated area C3.

21:43.770 --> 21:46.740
Groups in D4, remain on standby for now.

21:46.740 --> 21:50.980
Groups in E6, move north to pin him down.

21:53.140 --> 21:57.880
<i>Utomiya, Tsubaki, and Yagami have met up.</i>

21:57.880 --> 22:04.560
<i>And large numbers of first-years are 
pinning me in between D4 and E6.</i>

22:05.710 --> 22:07.880
I suppose it's time to make my move.
